Matrix operator regression
==========================

The full-system workflow runs two xsai-blas operators at three sizes each.
GEMM dimensions are M/K/N. FlashAttention dimensions are query length,
key/value length and head dimension.

    gemm_i8_f32       128/64/128     256/256/256    512/256/512
    flash_attention   8/130/70       32/256/64      256/512/128

Build DRAMsim3 as described in docs/quick_start.md. From the GEM5 root,
build GEM5 and run the small FlashAttention case.

    scons build/RISCV_MATRIX/gem5.opt --default=RISCV --enable-matrix --linker=gold -j64
    python3 .github/workflows/autotest/script/matrix_ci.py run \
        --case flash_attention-q8-kv130-d70 --output matrix-ci-results

Use --case gemm_i8_f32 or --case flash_attention to run all three sizes of
one operator. Omit --case to run all six images. The summary is in
matrix-ci-results/validation-results.json. Each entry includes the shape,
operator cycles, retired instructions and Matrix difftest counts. For a
failure, open runs/<case>/sim.log under the output directory. The exact
command is in command.json alongside it.

Inputs
------

    /nfs/share/gem5_ci/matrix/<case>-ci.bin
    /nfs/share/gem5_ci/ref/matrix/riscv64-nemu-interpreter-so

script/matrix_ci.py lists the six case IDs. Use --image-dir, --reference
and --gem5 to select other inputs or a different binary. The Matrix REF uses
a 1544-byte register layout.

What CI checks
--------------

gem5-matrix.yml runs on pushes to xs-dev and on manual dispatch. It runs two
cases at a time, with a 30-minute timeout per case, and uploads the logs and
summary as matrix-correctness-results.

Each guest runs the optimized Matrix and RVV implementation once and compares
the output against an embedded reference computed on the host. The guest must
reach m5_exit with NEMU difftest enabled. Every shape must have a checked
MMA and a completed Matrix memory request. At exit, submitted, completed and
checked commands must balance, every sent memory request must have a response,
and pendingChecks, pendingOwners and pendingMemory must all be zero.

The guest reads cycle and instret around xsai_op_plan_execute. This measures
one operator invocation with zero warmups. Plan creation, the host-reference
comparison and guest startup are outside the measured interval. The runner
requires one positive sample tagged with the requested shape and records it
in the performance field. There is no cycle threshold.

All six images use DRAMsim3 and --classic-l2. The large FlashAttention case
hits an express-snoop assertion in CoherentXBar::recvTimingSnoopResp with
the default XiangShan L2. FlashAttention also uses the SEW=16 RVV widening
conversion from #1372.

Run the result-parser tests with

    python3 -m unittest discover -s .github/workflows/autotest/script -p test_matrix_ci.py
